## Structure (vertical slices)

Each feature is a self-contained vertical slice — one folder that cuts through all layers:

```
src/features/<feature>/
├── <feature>.module.ts       ← NestJS module wiring
├── <feature>.controller.ts   ← HTTP layer (thin, no business logic)
├── <feature>.handler.ts      ← business logic / use-case
├── <feature>.repository.ts   ← data access
├── <feature>.entity.ts       ← domain model
├── create-<feature>.dto.ts   ← input validation / request shape
├── <feature>.response.ts     ← output DTO
└── <feature>.controller.spec.ts
```

Call direction: `controller` → `handler` → `repository`. Cross-cutting concerns
(lib, db, cache, auth) live in `src/shared/` and are imported by features through
the NestJS module system.

The repository is currently in-memory. To move to a real database, change the
repository implementation only — the handler and controller stay untouched.

